{"name":"Mistral","hex":"#b8bfcc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mistral","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A surname from French.","Frédéric Mistral (French writer)"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mistral"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mistral (wind)","blocks":[{"text":"The mistral is a strong, cold, northwesterly wind that blows from southern France into the Gulf of Lion in the northern Mediterranean. It produces sustained winds averaging 50 km/h (30 mph), sometimes reaching 100 km/h (60 mph). It can last for several days. Periods of the wind exceeding 30 km/h for more than sixty-five hours have been reported. It is most common in the winter and spring, and strongest in the transition between the two seasons."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Brosen_windrose.svg/330px-Brosen_windrose.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistral_(wind)","wikidata":"Q193742"},{"title":"Maserati Mistral","blocks":[{"text":"The Maserati Mistral is a 2-seat gran turismo produced by Italian car manufacturer Maserati between 1963 and 1970. The successor to the 3500 GT, it was styled by Frua and bodied by Maggiora of Turin. A total of 844 coupés and 124 Spyders were built."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5f/1967_Maserati_Mistral_Coupe_-_silver_-_fvr_%284637057473%29_cropped.jpg/330px-1967_Maserati_Mistral_Coupe_-_silver_-_fvr_%284637057473%29_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Maserati_Mistral","wikidata":"Q1907028"},{"title":"Mistral (missile)","blocks":[{"text":"The Missile Transportable Anti-aérien Léger, commonly called Mistral, is a family of French infrared homing multipurpose short range air defense system manufactured by MBDA France. Based on the French SATCP, the development of the portable system that would later become the Mistral began in 1974. The first version of the system was introduced in 1990, the second in 1998, and the third in 2013."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg/330px-Mistral_Atlas_launcher_of_the_Hungarian_Armed_Forces_cropped.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistral_(missile)","wikidata":"Q54225"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG/500px-Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG/1280px-Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/54/Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG/500px-Mistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mistral wind blowing near Marseille. In the centre is the Château d'If.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMistral_sur_le_Frioul.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Carte_du_mistral.png/500px-Carte_du_mistral.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f6/Carte_du_mistral.png/500px-Carte_du_mistral.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A map showing the force of the mistral one day in November 2008. The wind reached a speed of 80 km/h (50 mph), with average speeds of more than 50 km/h (31 mph) near Marseille.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACarte_du_mistral.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg/500px-Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg/1280px-Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/65/Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg/500px-Bell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d%27Azur_Provence_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The bell tower of the hilltop village of La Cadière-d'Azur is open, which allows the mistral to pass through.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABell_Tower_La_Cadiere_d'Azur_Provence_France.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Mistral_wind1.jpg/330px-Mistral_wind1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7f/Mistral_wind1.jpg/330px-Mistral_wind1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Schematic diagram of mistral wind occurrence in Europe.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMistral_wind1.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg/500px-Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg/1280px-Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg/500px-Gebogene_Korkeiche.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Oak bent to the south by the mistral in Sardinia","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGebogene_Korkeiche.jpg"}